#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr ""
"Un curso gratuito de IBM sobre información cuántica y computación cuántica"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Naimark's theorem"
msgstr "Teorema de Naimark"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore orthogonalization */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore orthogonalization */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Naimark's theorem* is a fundamental fact concerning measurements.\n"
"It states that every general measurement can be implemented in a simple way that's reminiscent of Stinespring representations of channels:\n"
"1. The system to be measured is first combined with an initialized workspace system, forming a compound system.\n"
"2. A unitary operation is then performed on the compound system.\n"
"3. Finally, the workspace system is *measured* with respect to a *standard basis measurement*, yielding the outcome of the original general measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"El *teorema de Naimark* es una afirmación fundamental sobre las mediciones.\n"
"Establece que cualquier medición general puede implementarse de una forma sencilla que recuerda a las representaciones de Stinespring de los canales:\n"
"1. El sistema a medir se combina primero con un sistema auxiliar inicializado, creando un sistema compuesto.\n"
"2. Luego se aplica una operación unitaria al sistema compuesto.\n"
"3. Finalmente, el sistema auxiliar se *mide* mediante una *medición en la base estándar*, lo que proporciona el resultado de la medición general original.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theorem statement and proof {#theorem-statement-and-proof}"
msgstr "Enunciado del teorema y demostración {#theorem-statement-and-proof}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let $\\mathsf{X}$ be a system and let $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ be a "
"collection of positive semidefinite matrices satisfying\n"
msgstr ""
"Sea $\\mathsf{X}$ un sistema y $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ una colección de "
"matrices positivas semidefinidas que satisfacen\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which is to say that they describe a measurement of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Also let $\\mathsf{Y}$ be a system whose classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ which is the set of possible outcomes of this measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"lo cual indica que describen una medición de $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Sea ademas $\\mathsf{Y}$ un sistema cuyo conjunto de estados clásicos es $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, es decir, el conjunto de posibles resultados de medición.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Naimark's theorem states that there exists a unitary operation $U$ on the "
"compound system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ so that the implementation "
"suggested by the following figure yields measurement outcomes that agree "
"with the given measurement $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\},$ meaning that the "
"probabilities for the different possible measurement outcomes are precisely "
"in agreement.\n"
msgstr ""
"El teorema de Naimark establece que existe una operación unitaria $U$ sobre "
"el sistema compuesto $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ tal que la implementación "
"que sugiere la siguiente figura produce resultados de medición que coinciden"
" con la medición dada $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ — es decir, las "
"probabilidades de los distintos resultados posibles de medición coinciden "
"exactamente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![An implementation of a general measurement as in Naimark's "
"theorem](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-"
"information/general-measurements/Naimark.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Una implementación de una medición general según el teorema de "
"Naimark](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-"
"information/general-measurements/Naimark.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, the system $\\mathsf{X}$ starts out in some arbitrary state $\\rho$ while $\\mathsf{Y}$ is initialized to the $\\vert 0\\rangle$ state.\n"
"The unitary operation $U$ is applied to $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ and then the system $\\mathsf{Y}$ is measured with a standard basis measurement, yielding some outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Para aclarar: el sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ comienza en un estado arbitrario $\\rho,$ mientras que $\\mathsf{Y}$ se inicializa en el estado $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"La operación unitaria $U$ se aplica a $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$, y luego el sistema $\\mathsf{Y}$ se mide con una medición en la base estándar, produciendo un resultado $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The system $\\mathsf{X}$ is pictured as part of the output of the circuit, but for now we won't concern ourselves with the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ after $U$ is performed, and can imagine that it is traced out.\n"
"We'll be interested in the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ after $U$ is performed later in the lesson, though.\n"
msgstr ""
"El sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ se muestra como parte de la salida del circuito, pero por ahora no nos preocupa el estado de $\\mathsf{X}$ después de la ejecución de $U$, y podemos imaginar que se traza sobre el.\n"
"Sin embargo, más adelante en la lección nos interesará el estado de $\\mathsf{X}$ después de la ejecución de $U$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An implementation of a measurement in this way is clearly reminiscent of a Stinespring representation of a channel, and the mathematical underpinnings are similar as well.\n"
"The difference here is that the workspace system is measured rather than being traced out like in the case of a Stinespring representation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tal implementación de una medición recuerda obviamente a una representación de Stinespring de un canal, y las bases matemáticas son similares.\n"
"La diferencia es que el sistema auxiliar aquí se mide, en lugar de trazarse sobre el como en el caso de una representación de Stinespring.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fact that every measurement can be implemented in this way is pretty "
"simple to prove, but we're going to need a fact concerning positive "
"semidefinite matrices first.\n"
msgstr ""
"El hecho de que cualquier medición pueda implementarse de esta manera es "
"bastante sencillo de demostrar, pero primero necesitamos una afirmación "
"sobre matrices positivas semidefinidas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Fact\">\n"
"Suppose $P$ is an $n \\times n$ positive semidefinite matrix. There exists a unique $n\\times n$ positive semidefinite matrix $Q$ for which $Q^2 = P.$ This unique positive semidefinite matrix is called the *square root* of $P$ and is denoted $\\sqrt{P}.$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Hecho\">\n"
"Sea $P$ una matriz positiva semidefinida $n \\times n$. Existe una única matriz positiva semidefinida $n\\times n$ $Q$ para la cual $Q^2 = P$. Esta única matriz positiva semidefinida se denomina la *raíz cuadrada* de $P$ y se denota $\\sqrt{P}$.\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to find the square root of a positive semidefinite matrix is to "
"first compute a spectral decomposition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una forma de encontrar la raíz cuadrada de una matriz positiva semidefinida "
"es calcular primero una descomposición espectral.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because $P$ is positive semidefinite, its eigenvalues must be nonnegative "
"real numbers, and by replacing them with their square roots we obtain an "
"expression for the square root of $P.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dado que $P$ es positiva semidefinida, sus valores propios deben ser números"
" reales no negativos, y reemplazándolos por sus raíces cuadradas obtenemos "
"una expresión para la raíz cuadrada de $P.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sqrt{P} = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sqrt{P} = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this concept in hand, we're ready to prove Naimark's theorem.\n"
"Under the assumption that $\\mathsf{X}$ has $n$ classical states, a unitary operation $U$ on the pair $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ can be represented by an $nm\\times nm$ matrix, which we can view as an $m\\times m$ block matrix whose blocks are $n\\times n.$\n"
"The key to the proof is to take $U$ to be any unitary matrix that matches the following pattern.\n"
msgstr ""
"Con este concepto, estamos listos para demostrar el teorema de Naimark.\n"
"Bajo la suposición de que $\\mathsf{X}$ tiene $n$ estados clásicos, una operación unitaria $U$ sobre el par $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ puede representarse mediante una matriz $nm\\times nm$, que podemos considerar como una matriz de bloques $m\\times m$ cuyos bloques son de tamaño $n\\times n$.\n"
"La clave de la demostración es elegir $U$ como cualquier matriz unitaria que siga el siguiente patrón.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For it to be possible to fill in the blocks marked with a question mark so that $U$ is unitary, it's both necessary and sufficient that the first $n$ columns, which are formed by the blocks $\\sqrt{P_0},\\ldots,\\sqrt{P_{m-1}},$ are orthonormal.\n"
"We can then use the Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process to fill in the remaining columns, just like we encountered in the previous lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para que sea posible rellenar los bloques marcados con signos de interrogación de modo que $U$ sea unitaria, es necesario y suficiente que las primeras $n$ columnas, formadas por los bloques $\\sqrt{P_0},\\ldots,\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}$, sean ortonormales.\n"
"Entonces podemos usar el proceso de ortogonalización de Gram-Schmidt para completar las columnas restantes, exactamente como en la lección anterior.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first $n$ columns of $U$ can be expressed as vectors in the following "
"way, where $c = 0,\\ldots,n-1$ refers to the column number starting from "
"$0.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Las primeras $n$ columnas de $U$ pueden expresarse como vectores de la "
"siguiente forma, donde $c = 0,\\ldots,n-1$ denota el número de columna "
"empezando desde $0$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_c\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\vert c\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_c\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\vert c\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can compute the inner product between any two of them as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Podemos calcular el producto interno entre cualesquiera dos de estos "
"vectores como sigue.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_c \\vert \\gamma_d \\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{a,b = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle \\cdot \\langle c \\vert \\sqrt{P_a}\\sqrt{P_b}\\, \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"= \\langle c \\vert \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a \\Biggr) \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"= \\langle c \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_c \\vert \\gamma_d \\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{a,b = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle \\cdot \\langle c \\vert \\sqrt{P_a}\\sqrt{P_b}\\, \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"= \\langle c \\vert \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a \\Biggr) \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"= \\langle c \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This shows that these columns are in fact orthonormal, so we can fill in the"
" remaining columns of $U$ in a way that guarantees the entire matrix is "
"unitary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto muestra que estas columnas son efectivamente ortonormales, de modo que "
"podemos completar las columnas restantes de $U$ para que la matriz completa "
"sea unitaria.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It remains to check that the measurement outcome probabilities for the simulation are consistent with the original measurement.\n"
"For a given initial state $\\rho$ of $\\mathsf{X},$ the measurement described by the collection $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ results in each outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ with probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Queda comprobar que las probabilidades de los resultados de medición de la simulación son consistentes con la medición original.\n"
"Para un estado inicial dado $\\rho$ de $\\mathsf{X}$, la medición descrita por la colección $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ produce cada resultado $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ con probabilidad $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To obtain the outcome probabilities for the simulation, let's first give the name $\\sigma$ to the state of $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ after $U$ has been performed.\n"
"This state can be expressed as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para obtener las probabilidades de los resultados de la simulación, llamemos primero $\\sigma$ al estado de $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ después de la ejecución de $U$.\n"
"Este estado puede expresarse como sigue.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma =\n"
"U \\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho\\bigr) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma =\n"
"U \\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho\\bigr) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Equivalently, in a block matrix form, we have the following equation.\n"
msgstr ""
"De forma equivalente, tenemos en forma de matriz de bloques la siguiente "
"ecuación.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sigma & =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\rho & 0 & \\cdots & 0 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\sqrt{P_1} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_{m-1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\fbox{?} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\fbox{?} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[5mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0}\\rho\\sqrt{P_0} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_0}\\rho\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\\rho\\sqrt{P_0} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\\rho\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sigma & =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\rho & 0 & \\cdots & 0 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\sqrt{P_1} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_{m-1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\fbox{?} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\fbox{?} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[5mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0}\\rho\\sqrt{P_0} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_0}\\rho\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\\rho\\sqrt{P_0} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\\rho\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that the entries of $U$ falling into the blocks marked with a question mark have no influence on the outcome by virtue of the fact that we're conjugating a matrix of the form $\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho$\n"
"— so the question mark entries are always multiplied by zero entries of $\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho$ when the matrix product is computed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Observa que las entradas de $U$ que caen en los bloques marcados con signos "
"de interrogación no influyen en el resultado, ya que estamos conjugando una "
"matriz de la forma $\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho$ — "
"las entradas con signos de interrogación siempre se multiplican por entradas"
" nulas de $\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho$ al calcular "
"el producto matricial.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we can analyze what happens when a standard basis measurement is performed on $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"The probabilities of the possible outcomes are given by the diagonal entries of the reduced state $\\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}}$ of $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora podemos analizar qué sucede cuando se realiza una medición en la base estándar sobre $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Las probabilidades de los resultados posibles están dadas por las entradas diagonales del estado reducido $\\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}}$ de $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}} = \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\Bigl(\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\\Bigr) \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}} = \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\Bigl(\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\\Bigr) \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In particular, using the cyclic property of the trace, we see that the "
"probability to obtain a given outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ is as "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Usando la propiedad cíclica de la traza, vemos en particular que la "
"probabilidad de obtener un resultado dado $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ es la "
"siguiente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\Bigl(\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}\\Bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\Bigl(\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}\\Bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This matches with the original measurement, establishing the correctness of "
"the simulation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto coincide con la medición original y confirma la corrección de la "
"simulación.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Non-destructive measurements {#non-destructive-measurements}"
msgstr "Mediciones no destructivas {#non-destructive-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So far in the lesson, we've concerned ourselves with *destructive* "
"measurements, where the output consists of the classical measurement result "
"alone and there is no specification of the post-measurement quantum state of"
" the system that was measured.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hasta ahora en la lección nos hemos ocupado de mediciones *destructivas*, en"
" las que la salida consiste únicamente en el resultado clásico de medición y"
" no se hace ninguna especificación sobre el estado cuántico del sistema "
"medido después de la medición.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Non-destructive* measurements, on the other hand, do precisely this.\n"
"Specifically, non-destructive measurements describe not only the classical measurement outcome probabilities, but also the state of the system that was measured conditioned on each possible measurement outcome.\n"
"Note that the term *non-destructive* refers to the *system* being measured but not necessarily its state, which could change significantly as a result of the measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Las mediciones *no destructivas*, en cambio, hacen exactamente eso.\n"
"Concretamente, las mediciones no destructivas describen no solo las probabilidades de los resultados clásicos de medición, sino también el estado del sistema medido, condicionado a cada resultado posible de medición.\n"
"Observa que el término *no destructiva* se refiere al *sistema* que se mide, no necesariamente a su estado, que podría cambiar considerablemente como resultado de la medición.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In general, for a given destructive measurement, there will be multiple (in fact infinitely many) non-destructive measurements that are *compatible* with the given destructive measurement, meaning that the classical measurement outcome probabilities match precisely with the destructive measurement.\n"
"So, there isn't a unique way to define the post-measurement quantum state of a system for a given measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"En general, para una medición destructiva dada, existen varias (de hecho infinitas) mediciones no destructivas que son *compatibles* con la medición destructiva dada, es decir, en las que las probabilidades de los resultados clásicos de medición coinciden exactamente con la medición destructiva.\n"
"Por tanto, no existe una forma única de definir el estado cuántico de un sistema después de una medición.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is, in fact, possible to generalize non-destructive measurements even "
"further, so that they produce a classical measurement outcome along with a "
"quantum state output of a system that isn't necessarily the same as the "
"input system.\n"
msgstr ""
"De hecho, es posible generalizar las mediciones no destructivas aun más, de "
"modo que produzcan un resultado clásico de medición junto con un estado "
"cuántico de salida de un sistema que no es necesariamente el mismo que el "
"sistema de entrada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The notion of a non-destructive measurement is an interesting and useful abstraction.\n"
"It should, however, be recognized that non-destructive measurements can always be described as compositions of channels and destructive measurements — so there is a sense in which the notion of a destructive measurement is the more fundamental one.\n"
msgstr ""
"El concepto de medición no destructiva es una abstracción interesante y útil.\n"
"Sin embargo, debe reconocerse que las mediciones no destructivas siempre pueden describirse como composiciones de canales y mediciones destructivas — en este sentido, el concepto de medición destructiva es el más fundamental.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "From Naimark's theorem {#from-naimarks-theorem}"
msgstr "A partir del teorema de Naimark {#from-naimarks-theorem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider the simulation of a general measurement like we have in Naimark's theorem.\n"
"A simple way to obtain a non-destructive measurement from this simulation is revealed by the figure from before, where the system $\\mathsf{X}$ is not traced out, but is part of the output.\n"
"This yields both a classical measurement outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ as well as a post-measurement quantum state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Consideremos la simulación de una medición general como en el teorema de Naimark.\n"
"Una forma sencilla de obtener una medición no destructiva a partir de está simulación se revela en la figura anterior, en la que el sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ no se traza sobre el, sino que forma parte de la salida.\n"
"Esto proporciona tanto un resultado clásico de medición $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ como un estado cuántico de $\\mathsf{X}$ después de la medición.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's describe these states in mathematical terms.\n"
"We're assuming that the initial state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\rho,$ so that after the initialized system $\\mathsf{Y}$ is introduced and $U$ is performed, we have that $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ is in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Describamos estos estados en términos matemáticos.\n"
"Suponemos que el estado inicial de $\\mathsf{X}$ es $\\rho$, de modo que tras introducir el sistema inicializado $\\mathsf{Y}$ y ejecutar $U$, el sistema $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ se encuentra en el estado\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma =\n"
"U \\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho\\bigr) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma =\n"
"U \\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho\\bigr) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The probabilities for the different classical outcomes to appear are the same as before — they can't change as a result of us deciding to ignore or not ignore $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"That is, we obtain each $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ with probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Las probabilidades de los distintos resultados clásicos son las mismas que antes — no pueden cambiar porque hayamos decidido ignorar o no ignorar $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Es decir, obtenemos cada $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ con probabilidad $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Conditioned upon having obtained a particular measurement outcome $a,$ the "
"resulting state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is given by this expression.\n"
msgstr ""
"Condicionado a un resultado de medición particular $a$, el estado resultante"
" de $\\mathsf{X}$ viene dado por esta expresión.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to see this is to represent a standard basis measurement of $\\mathsf{Y}$ by the completely dephasing channel $\\Delta_m,$ where the channel output describes classical measurement outcomes as (diagonal) density matrices.\n"
"An expression of the state we obtain is as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una forma de ver esto es representar una medición en la base estándar de $\\mathsf{Y}$ mediante el canal completamente defasante $\\Delta_m$, donde la salida del canal describe los resultados clásicos de medición como matrices de densidad (diagonales).\n"
"Una expresión del estado que obtenemos es la siguiente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\Delta_m(\\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert) \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\n"
"= \\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\Delta_m(\\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert) \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\n"
"= \\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can then write this state as a convex combination of product states,\n"
msgstr ""
"Entonces podemos escribir este estado como una combinación convexa de "
"estados producto,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\\, \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\\, \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which is consistent with the expression we've obtained for the state of "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ conditioned on each possible measurement outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"lo cual es consistente con la expresión que obtuvimos para el estado de "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ condicionado a cada resultado posible de medición.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "From a Kraus representation {#from-a-kraus-representation}"
msgstr ""
"A partir de una representación de Kraus {#from-a-kraus-representation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are alternative selections for $U$ in the context of Naimark's theorem"
" that produce the same measurement outcome probabilities but give entirely "
"different output states of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Existen elecciones alternativas para $U$ en el contexto del teorema de "
"Naimark que producen las mismas probabilidades de resultados de medición "
"pero estados de salida de $\\mathsf{X}$ completamente diferentes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For instance, one option is to substitute $(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes V) U$ for $U,$ where $V$ is any unitary operation on $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"The application of $V$ to $\\mathsf{X}$ commutes with the measurement of $\\mathsf{Y}$ so the classical outcome probabilities do not change, but now the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ conditioned on the outcome $a$ becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Una opción es, por ejemplo, sustituir $(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes V) U$ por $U$, donde $V$ es una operación unitaria arbitraria sobre $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"La aplicación de $V$ a $\\mathsf{X}$ conmuta con la medición de $\\mathsf{Y}$, de modo que las probabilidades de los resultados clásicos no cambian. Ahora el estado de $\\mathsf{X}$ condicionado al resultado $a$ será\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{V \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}V^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{V \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}V^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "More generally, we could replace $U$ by the unitary matrix\n"
msgstr "Más en general, podríamos reemplazar $U$ por la matriz unitaria\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert \\otimes V_a\\Biggr) U\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert \\otimes V_a\\Biggr) U\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for any choice of unitary operations $V_0,\\ldots,V_{m-1}$ on $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Again, the classical outcome probabilities are unchanged, but now the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ conditioned on the outcome $a$ becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"para una elección arbitraria de operaciones unitarias $V_0,\\ldots,V_{m-1}$ sobre $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"De nuevo, las probabilidades de los resultados clásicos no cambian, pero ahora el estado de $\\mathsf{X}$ condicionado al resultado $a$ será\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{V_a \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}V_a^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{V_a \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}V_a^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An equivalent way to express this freedom is connected with Kraus representations.\n"
"That is, we can describe an $m$-outcome non-destructive measurement of a system having $n$ classical states by a selection of $n\\times n$ Kraus matrices $A_0,\\ldots,A_{m-1}$ satisfying the typical condition for Kraus matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una forma equivalente de expresar esta libertad está relacionada con las representaciones de Kraus.\n"
"Es decir, podemos describir una medición no destructiva con $m$ resultados de un sistema con $n$ estados clásicos mediante una elección de matrices de Kraus $n\\times n$ $A_0,\\ldots,A_{m-1}$ que satisfacen la condición tipica para matrices de Kraus.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} A_a^{\\dagger} A_a = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} A_a^{\\dagger} A_a = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assuming that the initial state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\rho,$ the classical "
"measurement outcome is $a$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"Suponiendo que el estado inicial de $\\mathsf{X}$ es $\\rho$, el resultado "
"clásico de medición es $a$ con probabilidad\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(A_a \\rho A_a^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(A_a^{\\dagger} A_a \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(A_a \\rho A_a^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(A_a^{\\dagger} A_a \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and conditioned upon the outcome being $a$ the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ "
"becomes\n"
msgstr "y condicionado al resultado $a$, el estado de $\\mathsf{X}$ será\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{A_a \\rho A_a^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(A_a^{\\dagger}A_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{A_a \\rho A_a^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(A_a^{\\dagger}A_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that this is equivalent to choosing the unitary operation $U$ in "
"Naimark's theorem as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Observa que esto es equivalente a elegir la operación unitaria $U$ en el "
"teorema de Naimark como sigue.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_{0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_{0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous lesson we observed that the columns formed by the blocks $A_0,\\ldots,A_{m-1}$ are necessarily orthogonal, by virtue of the\n"
"condition $(1).$\n"
msgstr ""
"En la lección anterior observamos que las columnas formadas por los bloques "
"$A_0,\\ldots,A_{m-1}$ son necesariamente ortogonales, debido a la condición "
"$(1).$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generalizations {#generalizations}"
msgstr "Generalizaciones {#generalizations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are even more general ways to formulate non-destructive measurements than the ways we've discussed.\n"
"The notion of a *quantum instrument* (which won't be described here) represents one way to do this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Existen formas aun más generales de formular mediciones no destructivas que las discutidas.\n"
"El concepto de un *instrumento cuántico* (que no se describe aquí) representa una de tales posibilidades.\n"
